### The actual remaining bottleneck

**Multi-scene architecture.** Native cgame is live (`5977485`). cgame submits
~30-100 entities + 0-3 dlights + 0-1 polys per frame CORRECTLY, but ~95% of them
target HUD sub-scenes (rdflags=RDF_NOWORLDMODEL, tiny viewports: player portrait
head, rotating ammo pickup icon, weapon select bar, scoreboard, attacker face).
Our renderer's `RE_RenderScene` gates entity emission on `rdflags==0`, so HUD
sub-scenes are thrown away. The next `ClearScene` wipes them from the intake
before Swift reads. Need:

- Array of Q3MetalSceneSnapshot instead of single
- Per-scene viewport/origin/axis/fovX/fovY captured at RenderScene time
- Swift iterates scenes[], setViewport + setScissorRect per scene, renders each

Est. 200 lines C + 80 lines Swift. Unlocks HUD heads, rotating ammo pickups,
scoreboard portraits, attacker face, 3D menu models, viewmodel quad shell
(currently faked), eliminates the entire synthesizer bandage farm
(SynthesizeViewmodelEntity etc.).

