### 2026-04-21 follow-up session — explosion rectangle fix

Built on top of `22a938c`. Captured `demo four` runs side-by-side and caught
the "yellow rectangle around rocket explosion" regression that e95122a
triggered and 7eccf3a (narrow-synth) only partially addressed.

Root cause: Q3 explosion textures are uniformly bright yellow/orange blobs
that fill the texture without dark borders. The original .tga used a
circular alpha mask; the .jpg fallback has no alpha, and max(R,G,B)
recovers no mask when the texture is saturated.

Fix (`b936513`): combine luminance-alpha with a radial smoothstep mask
centered on the texture. Corners fade regardless of source content, and
alpha<24 pixels get their RGB zeroed out so JPG noise can't leak under
additive blends. Re-enabled broad allow-list (sprites/, models/weaphits/,
gfx/damage/, gfx/misc/, gfx/2d/, powerups/, menu/art/) now that the radial
mask makes it safe.

Verified on `20260421_164145_radial-mask`:
- Rocket explosions render round, not rectangular
- World stays visible through the fireball
- Plasma bolts, flares, quad shell unchanged (were already working)
- Smoke wisps look natural (no yellow rect)
- HUD portrait + weapon icon + score text all clean

